# This repo ships the workspace *system* only — the rules, commands, skills and
# scripts. Every directory below is tracked, and carries a README explaining
# what belongs in it; the contents stay local, because they describe private
# services and their production incidents.
#
# Note: each rule ignores `dir/*`, not `dir/` — git cannot re-include a file
# whose parent directory is excluded, so the README would vanish with it.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- checkouts --
# Canonical service checkouts, cloned per machine. Full clones of the private
# services, carrying their own .env files and service-account keys.
/repos/*
!/repos/README.md

# Task worktrees, created by .claude/scripts/space.sh and torn down at the end
# of a task. Every file inside belongs to a service repo, not to this one.
/spaces/*
!/spaces/README.md

# ----------------------------------------------------------------- task docs --
# One directory per task - prd.md, plan.md, log.md, testing.md. They narrate real
# bugs and fixes in the private services, so only the README is tracked.
/docs/*
!/docs/README.md

# Release runbooks: commit-level state across the private repos.
/release/*
!/release/README.md

# ----------------------------------------------------------------- tooling --
# Per-machine Claude Code overrides. settings.json is shared; .local is not.
.claude/settings.local.json

# Per-machine workspace settings - branch prefix, default base ref. Everyone
# has their own; .env.example is the tracked template. See .claude/scripts/config.sh.
/.env
!/.env.example

# ------------------------------------------------------------------- noise --
.DS_Store
*.swp
*~

.env